  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q7",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "$(13,85,n)$ is a Pythagorean triad. Find the value(s) of $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=84$ only. Taking $n$ as the largest number gives $\\sqrt{7394}$, which is not a whole number.",
      "worked": "If $85$ is the largest number:\n$$\\begin{align*}13^2+n^2&=85^2\\\\n^2&=85^2-13^2\\\\n^2&=7225-169\\\\n&=\\sqrt{7056}=84\\end{align*}$$\nIf $n$ is the largest number:\n$$\\begin{align*}13^2+85^2&=n^2\\\\n^2&=169+7225\\\\n&=\\sqrt{7394}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $85^2<7394<86^2$, $\\sqrt{7394}$ is not a whole number. Therefore, $n=84$ is the only answer.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
